WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.734
-Welcome back, everybody. I'm
hanging out with Demi Lovato.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.567
Now, Demi --
New album this Friday.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:08.167
"Holy F."

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:10.067
We always have fun
when you're on the show,

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:11.834
so I wanted to play
a new game with you.

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:14.567
This is called "Quicktionary."
Here we go.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:19.367
-♪ It's Quick...tionary ♪

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:21.100
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.434
We each have a stack of cards
with clues on them, okay?

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:25.267
We're going to take turns
picking a card,

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.934
and then we're gonna
have to draw whatever clue

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:30.067
is on the card, but we'll only
have 10 seconds to draw.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.501
So you got to be quick. Okay?
-Okay.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.400
-And then, after that,
the drawing will come up

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.200
on the screen behind us,
and the other person

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.501
will have 10 seconds
to guess what that is.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:39.434
Quicktionary. Here we go.

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:42.367
For round one,
the category is songs.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.334
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.834
What song you thinking of --
Before we even see the clue?

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.133
What song do you think it is?

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.767
-What?!
-No, I'm just kidding.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:52.834
-Alright. That's a psychic game.
We'll play that next time.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.467
-Okay.
-You're our guest.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:57.467
Alright. That's the clue.
Don't show me. Look at the clue.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.567
When you're ready, say, "I'm
ready," and then start drawing.

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:02.467
And you have 10 seconds.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.601
-These are songs? Okay.

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:06.834
-Yeah. It's just one song.
Yeah.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.567
-Okay.
-Yep.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.067
10 seconds. Wow.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.634
-Oh, 10 seconds.
I'm so -- Wait.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:15.267
-No, it's happening.
It's 5 seconds now. Four...

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.801
Alright, we're getting
close to the end, there.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:18.634
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:19.767
Okay.
-Aah!

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:20.901
-No.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.334
That's good.
Let's see what you drew.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:24.467
And I have 10 seconds to guess.
Here we go.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:28.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:31.033
-First block. First square.

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.067
First -- One Direction? No.

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:36.934
First base. First --
That's not a song.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.501
"First Class."
-Yes!

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:41.634
-Wow.
-Yes! Yes!

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.067
I did not know
what to draw there.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:46.033
-I don't think you can
write the word "first,"

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.701
but I could be wrong.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:50.434
That kind of feels like
cheating to me.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.734
-Now that you say it out loud.
-Yeah, you go, "Oh."

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:56.033
You just wrote "First Class."
Awesome. Good clues.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.601
"How did I guess that one,
Jimmy? Oh, my gosh."

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:01.100
"Well, I wrote 'First Class.'"
Here we go. Songs.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.234
-Okay. Songs.
-Yeah, you got this.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.767
-I got this.
-Alright.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.200
Do I have to look away?

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.267
-No, you don't, but I'm ready.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:10.567
Go.

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:14.901
♪♪

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:19.200
♪♪

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.501
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:24.501
-Okay.
-Let's see what I drew.

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:26.100
-Okay.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.534
Love house.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:33.968
Love...home.

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.434
Love -- Heart.

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.067
Love...

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:39.334
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.501
Shack!
-Yes!

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.100
Come on! We got...

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.334
I could have drawn
Shaquille O'Neal,

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:49.167
but I'm not that talented.

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.667
But -- Okay. Your turn.

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.534
-Okay.
-Alright.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:55.734
Now, this one is TV shows.

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:57.734
-Okay.

00:02:57.734 --> 00:03:00.133
-TV show. I'm not looking.
But we got this.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.601
Come on.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:04.167
Partner, we've done this --
A thousand times, we've played.

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:07.100
Oh, you're going. Oh, sorry.
No, that's good. You're right.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.501
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:09.767
TV shows.

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.067
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:14.868
Okay. Okay.
Let's see what you did.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:17.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:18.701
Winnie the Pooh?

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.067
-It's -- No.
-"The Bear."

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.434
♪♪

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.267
Bear...Grylls? No.
[ Bell dinging ]

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:26.467
Bear -- Bear --

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.200
-Yes!
-Yes?

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.667
-Bear...
-Yay! "The Bear."

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.634
-"The Bear."
Oh, yeah! "The Bear." We got it.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:36.601
[ Dinging ]

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.601
Okay. Here we go.
Ready for this?

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.567
-Yeah.

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:42.033
-Gosh.

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:44.634
[ Breathes deeply ]

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:46.167
Okay.

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:54.300
♪♪

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.634
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.934
That was 10 seconds?

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:01.300
Alright. Let's see what I drew.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.801
-Okay.

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:06.567
Oh. Candles? Cake?

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:10.767
Birthday cake? The cake.
The candles.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.868
What?

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:14.033
Ohh...

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:15.968
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:18.367
Blowing out candles.
-No.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:21.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:24.267
You said it was cake.
-Yes.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.167
-But...

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.567
-Whose cake.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.501
-Not --
"Whose Cake?" is not a show.

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:31.968
"Whose Cake?" isn't...

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.000
"Is It Cake?"

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.200
-"Is It Cake?"
-"Is It Cake?" is a show.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.834
-Okay.
-Alright. Here we go.

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:39.868
The last one, we're going to
do this together, okay?

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.501
-Okay.
-Take this. That's for you.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:43.334
-Okay.
-This is for me, here.

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:44.968
We're gonna do this together.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:48.701
The category is
popular sayings, okay?

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:50.901
We're going to both write
on our iPads.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:52.267
It will go on the same screen.

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.734
And we're going to have to
get Questlove to guess.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.767
-[ Inhales sharply ]
Ah. Okay.

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:58.834
-And if he gets this right,
we're BFFs forever.

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:00.467
-And this is the hint?
-This is the hint.

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:01.567
This is it.
-Okay. Okay.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.067
-It's not even the hint.
This is it.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:04.501
-This is it.
Well, yes, this is --

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:06.400
-Are you ready?
-Yes.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.968
[ Laughs ]

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:11.434
-Ooh!
-Oh, it's a popular saying.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:16.200
♪♪

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.968
♪♪

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:23.133
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.801
Whew.
-Wow.

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:26.000
-Nailed it.
-Yeah.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.634
-You.
-Thank you.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.734
You did, too.
Yours was in the action of it.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.701
So that was better.
-Alright. Here we go.

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:33.934
Quest, come on, bud.
This is for all the money.

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:36.601
-Oh, boy. Oh, my God!

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:37.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.834 --> 00:05:39.868
Is that a bleeding heart?
-No.

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:41.767
[ Laughter ]
-No.

00:05:41.767 --> 00:05:43.167
-Is that a puppy?
-Five seconds.

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:44.968
It's not a puppy.
-Is that an axe?

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.434
-Keep saying stuff.
-No!

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:47.567
-Flag.
-No.

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:49.000
-Mongoose.
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.400
Wait a minute!
Ten seconds is too short.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.400
-A mongoose?
Where do you see mongoose?

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.434
-I don't know.
It looks like --

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:58.033
-That is fantastic.
Good job on your part.

00:05:58.033 --> 00:06:01.300
That is clearly a tea bag.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.634
Now do you guess it?

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:07.133
-Tea bag -- No.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.434
Oh, uh, uh, it's a saying.

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:13.567
A cup of tea. A spot of tea.

00:06:13.567 --> 00:06:16.167
Oh, spill the tea!
-Yes!

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.734
-There we go. Yay!

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:22.133
-I'm gonna take that.
Demi Lovato, everybody.

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:26.234
Demi's "Holy F" tour

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:28.701
is going on through this fall.

00:06:28.701 --> 00:06:31.901
Their album is out this Friday!

00:06:31.901 --> 00:06:34.267
When we come back, we're talking
with Murray Bartlett.

00:06:34.267 --> 00:06:36.801
Stick around, everybody.
This Friday! Come on!

